# Model self-activation of skills (ADR 0020) — implementation evidence (2026-07-20)
# Invariant carried forward from ADR 0019: a skill is ADVISORY procedural
# knowledge, never authorizing — even when the MODEL flips it on itself.

== Review criteria, point by point ==

(a) Model self-activates → sees instructions next step → urged IN-space
    action executes:
    test model_self_activates_skill_then_urged_action_executes (crates/
    skills/tests/skills_test.rs). A `SelfActivatingOracle` proposes
    `activate_skill(urge-echo)` with NOTHING operator-activated; the kernel
    executes it as a kernel-owned action (no tool call); on the NEXT step the
    oracle's guidance now contains "USE ACTION: echo" (proof the instructions
    only became visible after the kernel applied the activation), proposes
    `echo`, and it runs through the unchanged validate->execute path.
    Live transcript: see "== Demo transcript ==" scenario 1 below —
    `step 0: Executed activate_skill ... trust":"untrusted" ...` then
    `step 1: Executed echo ok=true`.

(b) THE INVARIANT holds under MODEL activation (not just operator
    activation): a self-activated skill urging an out-of-space action is
    still rejected.
    test invariant_holds_under_model_self_activation — extends the ADR 0019
    invariant test to route activation through the model's own
    `activate_skill` proposal rather than the operator CLI. `wipe_disk` is
    proposed (so the model really did learn the name only from the
    now-visible body) and the kernel schema-validation rejects it
    ("proposed action 'wipe_disk' is not in the action space"); the run
    still completes (the oracle falls back to `finish`); `wipe_disk` never
    appears as an executed step.
    Live transcript: scenario 2 below.

(c) Run-scoped and ephemeral: never mutates the operator's persistent
    registry state or a skill's trust; a fresh run starts empty.
    test self_activation_is_run_scoped_and_ephemeral — after a run
    self-activates `urge-echo`, `reg.active_names()` and
    `reg.trust_of("urge-echo")` are asserted UNCHANGED from before the run
    (no `active.toml` write, no sidecar write); a second, freshly-created run
    is asserted to have `active_skills.is_empty()`.
    Live transcript: every scenario below prints `operator active_names=[]`
    both before and after the run self-activates something.

(d) The budget is a hard floor — refusal, never silent overflow.
    test budget_refuses_activation_that_would_exceed_the_cap — three 16 KiB
    (post-truncation) skills are operator-activated (already at the 48 KiB
    cap); the gate's `authorize_activation` is asserted to return `Err`
    directly, AND through the kernel: a `Rejected` event fires and
    `run.active_skills` never contains the refused skill (no state change).
    Live transcript: scenario 3 below —
    `Rejected activating 'big4' would push the total advisory-instruction
    budget to 65616 bytes, over the 49152 byte cap`.

(e) Deactivate: activate then deactivate -> instructions gone next step.
    test deactivate_removes_instructions_next_step — a dedicated oracle
    activates on step 0, checks `context.guidance` for a body marker on step
    1 (asserted PRESENT), deactivates, checks again on step 2 (asserted
    ABSENT). Asserts the collected sequence is exactly `[true, false]`.

(f) Trust policy: `TrustedOnly` refuses an untrusted skill (every skill is
    untrusted at install — ADR 0019 unchanged), `All` permits.
    test trust_policy_trusted_only_refuses_untrusted_all_permits — a unit
    test directly on `RegistrySkillGate`: `TrustedOnly.any_activatable()` is
    false with only an untrusted skill installed (the feature is INERT by
    default, as designed); `authorize_activation` under `TrustedOnly`
    returns `Err` mentioning "trust"; under `All`, `any_activatable()` is
    true and `authorize_activation` returns `Ok("untrusted")`.

(No regression, mirroring ADR 0019's §7.6): propose->validate->execute and
`ValidatedAction` untouched — the model-activation seam is a new trait
(`kernel_core::SkillGate`) plus one inline branch in the engine loop next to
`finish`; `ActionSchema::validate` itself was not modified beyond the crate
adding the two new specs to the offered schema. `cargo test --workspace`:
157 passed (36 suites) — 151 pre-existing (per the ADR 0019 evidence log) + 6
new skills tests. `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`:
clean. `cargo fmt --all`: clean (no diffs after running).

