== Demo transcript (`cargo run -p skills --example model-activation-demo`) ==
A real kernel run (in-memory store, mock oracle, no daemon) with the actual
event stream printed — Proposed -> Executed(trust) and the invariant
rejection, not just test pass/fail:

=== scenario: self-activate then urged in-space action ===
installed 'urge-echo' (trust: untrusted) — NOT operator-activated
  step 0: Proposed  activate_skill
  step 0: Executed  activate_skill ok=true result={"activated":"urge-echo","trust":"untrusted","run_active":["urge-echo"]}
  step 1: Proposed  echo
  step 1: Executed  echo ok=true result={"echoed":"from self-activated skill"}
  step 2: Proposed  finish
run status=Completed run.active_skills=["urge-echo"] operator active_names=[]

=== scenario: invariant: self-activated skill urging an out-of-space action ===
installed 'urge-forbidden' (trust: untrusted) — NOT operator-activated
  step 0: Proposed  activate_skill
  step 0: Executed  activate_skill ok=true result={"activated":"urge-forbidden","trust":"untrusted","run_active":["urge-forbidden"]}
  step 1: Proposed  wipe_disk
  step 1: Rejected  proposed action 'wipe_disk' is not in the action space
  step 1: Proposed  finish
run status=Completed run.active_skills=["urge-forbidden"] operator active_names=[]

=== scenario: budget refusal (hard floor) ===
operator-active: ["big1", "big2", "big3"] (each ~16 KiB post-truncation; 3 * 16 KiB = 48 KiB = the cap)
  step 0: Proposed  activate_skill
  step 0: Rejected  activating 'big4' would push the total advisory-instruction budget to 65616 bytes, over the 49152 byte cap — deactivate something first
  step 0: Proposed  finish
run status=Completed run.active_skills=[] (big4 must be absent)

