== Deviations / notes for Eryk ==

1. OPEN DECISION (not resolved silently, per the task brief): the default
   `[skills] model_activation` policy. Shipped default is "trusted" (the
   feature is INERT until you explicitly trust a skill via the sidecar file
   — every skill is untrusted at install). "all" is available and equally
   safe capability-wise (activation is still knowledge only); the
   difference is steering risk, not capability risk. See ADR 0020's
   "Policy knob" section for the full trade-off.
2. Desktop (`apps/desktop`) is NOT wired to this feature, matching the fact
   that it already does not wire skills or learned-facts at all. Noted in
   the ADR as a deferred, mechanical follow-up.
3. The `tmp()` test helper in `crates/skills/tests/skills_test.rs` had a
   latent uniqueness bug (pid + nanosecond timestamp could collide under
   parallel test threads) that a flaky failure surfaced once this change
   grew the suite from 9 to 15 tests. Fixed with an added monotonic counter
   — a test-infrastructure fix, not a production-code change.
4. No new `RunEvent` variant was added for activation; `Executed` carries
   the trust label in its `result` JSON. Judged sufficient to keep the event
   surface small (see ADR 0020, Consequences/Deferred).
